---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import SceneHead from "../components/SceneHead.astro";
---
<Base title="About: amader.cloud" description="Why we give old devices a second job, the rules we hold ourselves to, and what we count.">
<section class="page-head photo">
<SceneHead id="teastall" />
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>Dhaka already owns the hardware.</h1>
    <p class="name-line">The name: "amader" means "ours". The devices, the data and the network belong to the people who use them.</p>
    <p class="lede">Most homes here have a drawer of devices that still work: the TV box from before the smart TV, the phone from before the last phone, the office laptop that got replaced. They don't need a factory, only someone to wipe them, rebuild them and look after them. That's us.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap stack" style="padding-bottom:clamp(56px,8vw,112px)">
  <div class="split">
    <div>
      <svg class="pict" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#p-home"/></svg><h2>Why "amader"</h2>
      <p>It means "ours". The devices are yours, the data is yours, and the network is something the members of a building or a neighbourhood own together. We run the service, but we never hold your devices hostage. Cancel and you keep everything.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <svg class="pict" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#p-shield"/></svg><h2>What we hold ourselves to</h2>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li>We reuse before we recycle, and we recycle only through formal recyclers.</li>
        <li>Every device gets a record of how it was wiped.</li>
        <li>We publish only figures we've measured, with no estimates passed off as results.</li>
        <li>We never let anyone use a member's internet connection as a proxy.</li>
        <li>If we can't keep a device secure, we retire it.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2>What we count</h2>
    <p class="measure">Every device we handle gets a passport: what it is, how it was wiped, what job it has now, how much power it draws. These numbers come straight from those records. They start at zero because our pilot hasn't started yet.</p>
    <ul class="ledger">
      <li><div class="fig">0<small>devices with a second job</small></div><div><p>Counting starts with our first pilot building.</p></div></li>
      <li><div class="fig">0<small>devices sent to formal recyclers</small></div><div><p>Each with a recycler's receipt.</p></div></li>
      <li><div class="fig">—<small>average watts per device type</small></div><div><p>We'll publish these once we've metered pilot devices for a month.</p></div></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="panel-dusk cta">
    <div>
      <h2>Work with us</h2>
      <p style="margin:0">We're looking for pilot buildings, a company with devices to retire, a school that wants a lab, and technicians who like fixing things.</p>
    </div>
    <a class="btn btn-bulb" href="contact.html">Get in touch</a>
  </div>
</section>
</Base>
